# Stability checklist

Every crash-prevention rule from the project brief, where it is enforced in code, how it is tested,
and what has actually been verified. File references are generated by `tools/gen_stability_doc.py`
(CI fails if they drift).

**Verification legend**

- **Ran here**: exercised by tests that ran on Linux (GCC 13 with ASan/UBSan/LSan, Clang 18, clang-tidy).
- **Mock-compiled**: the After Effects glue compiles against `tools/ae_sdk_mock`. That catches C++ errors, not SDK signature mismatches.
- **Windows/AE pending**: needs the real AE SDK, MSVC, an NVIDIA GPU or After Effects itself. Not run yet.

## 1. No exception ever escapes a host callback

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Every `PF_Cmd_*` goes through one dispatcher wrapped in `try`/`catch` (`PF_Err`, `bad_alloc`, `std::exception`, `...`) | {{ref:effectmain_try}}, {{ref:effectmain_catch}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled; Windows/AE pending |
| Errors become `out_data->return_msg` through the host `ansi.sprintf`, truncated first (that sprintf is unbounded) | {{ref:report_message}}, {{ref:sprintf}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| Every exported engine function runs inside `guard()`, which maps any exception to a `dms_status`. The C ABI is `extern "C"` and returns codes only | {{ref:guard}} | `EngineLifecycle.*`, every engine test | Ran here |
| The render pipeline is `noexcept` and always leaves a valid output buffer | {{ref:render_noexcept}} | `PluginCore.*`, `PixelDepthTest.*` | Ran here |
| Rotating log, 5 × 2 MiB, in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\DMS\logs` (`~/.local/state/dms/logs` on Linux) | {{ref:logger_rotate}} | used by all tests | Ran here (Linux path) |

## 2. GPU failures fall back, never return garbage

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Plan: requested → FP32 (if FP16 failed) → lower base resolution → more tiles at smaller per-tile resolution → CPU | {{ref:fallback_plan}} | `BackendPlan.NvidiaChainOrder`, `BackendPlan.*` | Ran here |
| Executor walks the plan. Only OOM, backend, load and inference failures advance it. Abort and timeout stop it | {{ref:fallback_loop}} | `FallbackFixture.*` (injected CUDA OOM, driver failure, FP16 NaN) | Ran here, with simulated GPU |
| Non-finite model output (FP16 overflow) is treated as a failure and triggers the FP32 rung | {{ref:nonfinite_out}} | `FallbackFixture.Fp16NonFiniteOutputFallsBackToFp32` | Ran here |
| Last rungs: the instance's last good depth, else a flat mid-gray map plus one user message | {{ref:render_fallback}} | `PluginCore.MissingModelRendersGrayAndReportsOnce`, `PluginCore.FailureAfterSuccessUsesLastGoodDepth` | Ran here |
| An OOM rung is not retried every frame (30 s memo) | {{ref:oom_memo}} | `FallbackFixture.CudaOomFallsBackToCpuWithMessage` | Ran here |
| Error messages are de-duplicated per instance, so there is no dialog per frame | {{ref:message_dedup}} | `InstanceRegistry.LastGoodDepthAndMessageDedup` | Ran here |
| Corrupt or truncated model files are rejected before session creation (size check; SHA-256 at download and on demand) | {{ref:model_size_check}} | `EngineInference.CorruptOrIncompatibleModelFailsCleanly` | Ran here |

