| `PF_Handle` ownership (`HostHandle`, `HandleLock`) | {{ref:raii_handle}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| SmartFX layer checkouts are always checked back in | {{ref:raii_checkout}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| `PF_CHECKOUT_PARAM` is always paired with `PF_CHECKIN_PARAM` | {{ref:raii_param}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| Pre-render data is owned by `unique_ptr` until handed to the host, and the host deleter reclaims it | {{ref:prerender_owner}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| `grep` for `new`, `malloc` and `free(` in `plugin/` finds nothing | n/a | review | Ran here |

## 6. Flattenable sequence data and cross-version projects

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Sequence data is a 96-byte POD with no pointers; in-memory and flat forms are identical | {{ref:seq_struct}} | `SequenceData.RoundTripAndForeignVersions` | Ran here |
| Upgrade accepts older, newer, truncated, oversized-declared and garbage data | {{ref:seq_upgrade}} | `SequenceData.RoundTripAndForeignVersions` | Ran here |
| RESETUP always allocates a fresh handle; FLATTEN returns the flat handle; GET_FLATTENED returns a new copy | {{ref:seq_resetup}}, {{ref:seq_flatten}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled; Windows/AE pending |
| Render threads read sequence data only through `PF_GetConstSequenceData` (MFR) | {{ref:seq_const}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |

## 7. Process-wide engine singleton, never per instance or per frame

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| One refcounted engine behind a mutex; handles are validated, and in-flight calls hold a `shared_ptr` | {{ref:singleton}}, {{ref:acquire}}, {{ref:lock_engine}} | `EngineLifecycle.*` (including concurrent acquire/release) | Ran here |
| ORT env, sessions and CUDA arena live on one worker thread. They are created lazily and cached across instances | {{ref:worker}} | `EngineInference.ConcurrentRendersAreSerializedSafely` | Ran here (CPU EP) |
| Released at `PF_Cmd_GLOBAL_SETDOWN` | {{ref:global_setdown}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| ORT and driver libraries are loaded once and never unloaded (unloading leaks their static state and is unsafe) | {{ref:dll_pin}} | LSan-clean test runs | Ran here |
| Windows DLL hygiene: dependencies are pre-loaded by full path from `DMS_deps`, so System32, `PATH` and the AE folder are never searched; a foreign `onnxruntime.dll` is logged | {{ref:dll_preload}} | `tools/check_deps.py` on the real fetched layout (all imports resolved) | Layout checked here; loading Windows/AE pending |

## 8. Driver compatibility

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Policy constants: CUDA needs driver 527.41 or newer; Memory Sharing needs 560.00 or newer | {{ref:driver_policy}} | `BackendPlan.OldDriverSkipsCudaAndUsesDirectMLIfAvailable` | Ran here |
| Driver too old means CUDA is never attempted (the `cudaErrorInsufficientDriver` case) and this is logged | {{ref:insufficient_driver}} | `FallbackFixture.OldDriverNeverTriesCudaAndMemShareIsDisabled` | Ran here (fake GPU) |
| Memory Sharing is silently disabled on older drivers and logged once | {{ref:memshare_disable}} | same | Ran here |
| CUDA initialization failure at runtime disables CUDA for the session (sticky) | {{ref:sticky}} | `FallbackFixture.InsufficientDriverIsStickyAndSilentAfterFirstFrame` | Ran here |

## 9. Concurrent SMART_RENDER (MFR)

| What | Where | Tested by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bounded queue with condition-variable waits and timeouts, no spinning | {{ref:queue}} | `EngineInference.ConcurrentRendersAreSerializedSafely` (8 threads × 10 frames) | Ran here |
| Jobs own their buffers (`shared_ptr`), so a caller that times out never leaves dangling pointers | {{ref:job_owns}} | ASan runs | Ran here |
| Mutable state is shared only behind locks (frame cache, instance registry, plane stores, buffer pool); the GPU driver table is initialized once, then immutable | {{ref:pool}}, {{ref:gpu_once}} | `FrameCache.ConcurrentAccessIsSafe` | Ran here |
| Flags `SUPPORTS_THREADED_RENDERING` and `SUPPORTS_GET_FLATTENED_SEQUENCE_DATA`; the PiPL and `GLOBAL_SETUP` flags are `static_assert`ed equal | {{ref:pipl_assert}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |
| `NON_PARAM_VARY` is set dynamically only for the temporal model | {{ref:dynamic_flags}} | mock compile | Mock-compiled |

